            <ArticleTitle>Unusual cause of persistent abdominal pain in a young girl: solid-pseudopapillary tumour of the pancreas (2006: 11b).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>567-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A solid-pseudopapillary tumour, a rare disease of the pancreas, in a young woman is presented. Since treatment involves complete excision of the mass, an early diagnosis is crucial to allow the curative resection.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
